            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0308" n="192" xml:id="pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.911/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Gonzales.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 98.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 28, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 123
                    of the 11th instant inclosing a copy of a letter addressed by you to President
                    Menocal, in which you stated that the time already served by Enrique Maza might
                    well be considered by the Cuban Government as sufficient satisfaction of his
                    sentence, and that this Government had no desire for his longer confinement.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your action.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
